    0.32–  6.25  шаг  6.75 с  This is Orchestra: one dashboard that runs a whole team of AI coding agents on your repository.
    7.06– 10.17  шаг  3.92 с  You describe the job to one orchestrator, in plain words.
   10.98– 15.27  шаг  5.11 с  It reads the code, finds the cause, and splits the work into parallel tracks.
   16.09– 20.23  шаг  4.96 с  Each track goes to its own worker, on its own git branch, so they never collide.
   21.05– 26.26  шаг  6.03 с  Mix models freely. Opus plans, Sonnet and Codex do the work, Haiku keeps the docs.
   27.08– 31.38  шаг  5.12 с  Click any worker to jump into its own chat, with its branch, context and cost.
   32.19– 36.90  шаг  5.52 с  You say go. The worker reports back with the files it changed and its test results.
   37.72– 41.66  шаг  4.76 с  The orchestrator reviews the diff, live, and runs the whole test suite itself.
   42.48– 46.66  шаг  5.00 с  Only then does it merge: one squash commit per task, and nothing is deployed.
   47.48– 49.13  шаг  2.47 с  The task board keeps up by itself.
   49.95– 53.57  шаг  4.44 с  Click the quota bar, and every Claude and Codex limit unfolds.
   54.39– 58.48  шаг  4.91 с  Each window keeps its history, so you see how fast it burns, week by week.
   59.30– 63.11  шаг  4.63 с  One more click opens the spend: cost per day, Claude and Codex stacked.
   63.93– 67.21  шаг  4.10 с  Switch to thirty days, or break it down by agent and model.
   68.03– 70.81  шаг  3.60 с  A gate holds new workers back before a limit is hit.
   71.63– 74.47  шаг  3.66 с  Anything risky, like moving money, waits for your OK.
   75.29– 80.42  шаг  7.95 с  Orchestra. Open source, self hosted, and it runs on the subscriptions you already have.
